course: dictionary
lesson: 12215
title: Joining things together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To conjoin means to join two or more things together so they become one. It is a formal word, so you will meet it more in books, news and science than in everyday chat. «The new bridge will conjoin the two towns.» The bridge joins the towns, so conjoin means join together.
explain: You may hear «conjoined twins» on the news. These are twins whose bodies are joined together at some part. Doctors sometimes carry out operations to separate them. The word is about a join that is there from birth.
explain: Grammar has a word from the same root: a conjunction. Conjunctions join ideas in a sentence, such as and, but and because. «I like tea, but I prefer milk.» Here but joins two ideas. Once you know conjoin means join, conjunction is easier to remember.
fact: Conjoin is a verb: conjoin, conjoins, conjoined, conjoining.
fact: «Conjoin» means to join two or more things together into one.
fact: «Conjoined twins» are twins born with their bodies joined together at some part.
fact: Conjunctions such as and, but and because come from the same root, and they join ideas in sentences.
fact: «Conjoined with» means joined together with something else.
exercise: «The new tunnel will conjoin the two towns.» What does conjoin mean here? | Wreck or destroy the two towns | *Join the two towns together | Hide the two towns from view | Measure the distance between the two towns
exercise: «She wanted to go, but it was raining.» Which word is a conjunction that joins two ideas? | she | *but | raining | wanted
exercise: Which word is the past tense of conjoin? | conjoin | conjoins | conjoining | *conjoined
test: «The two ideas were conjoined in one clear sentence.» What does conjoined mean? | Separated and split apart | Lost for ever | *Joined together | Written in pencil
test: «Doctors may separate conjoined twins with an operation.» What are conjoined twins? | Twins who look exactly the same | Twins who have never met | Twins who live in different countries | *Twins whose bodies are joined together at some part
exam: «Ellie wants to conjoin her two ideas into one story.» Which option best matches conjoin? | To ask a question | To forget something completely | To draw a picture | *To join two ideas together
